        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I understand your points, but I'd still like to challenge them.\r\n\r\n1. As I understand, the complexity emerges from the reliance on `ino` and `dev`. The usage of these fields can certainly be described in the commit body or in a code comment to make it easier to understand for future readers. I can also explore other options if you still believe it's too complex to accept.\r\n2. Re: performance. I imagine this plugin is not used in an environment where a move operation is executed _a lot_. It's an occasional operation. Is performance truly a concern? If you're willing to accept _a fix_ (doesn't have to be this one), I'd be ready to explore other solutions if you could describe in more detail what the use case is where performance would be a concern.\r\n3. This plugin supports renaming, but it simply doesn't work on my filesystem (the most common one used on Macs) in this use case. I've run into this often enough by now that I decided to open this PR. Maybe I'm particularly weird in that I have to do this type of rename :D, but I've experienced this _many times_ by now. I wouldn't invest my own time into this if I didn't have a use case where I felt the pain.\r\n\r\nUp to you, but I'm ready to adjust the PR and work for a solution, because I really do care about fixing this (as said, I've ran into this issue many times by now).",
