        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I'll point out that the docs aren't super-reassuring on `fname_case`:\r\n> Case in file names matters (for Darwin and MS-Windows this is not present).\r\n\r\nIf it just checks whether I'm on Darwin and not the filesystem itself, then it's not strictly correct. [Zed for example handles it correctly](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/e1a09e290c48fc02d07aaf2150856d77996414df/crates/fs/src/fs.rs#L1160-L1196) (although the solution is quite... interesting :D).",
            "created_at": "2026-01-02T15:08:47Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2203#issuecomment-3705551402",
            "id": 3705551402,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2203",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOFoksYM7c3joq",
