        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> If it just checks whether I'm on Darwin and not the filesystem itself, then it's not strictly correct.\r\n\r\nYes, [indeed](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/612cd99a00174fc8c12a439781e7108a6efa8bea/build.zig#L215) it [does](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/612cd99a00174fc8c12a439781e7108a6efa8bea/CMakeLists.txt#L119-L122).\r\n\r\n> Maybe it is indeed a hairy-enough issue to leave it unsolved. _Failing_ the rename is more safe than risking overwriting another file in case the user is renaming things on a case-sensitive filesystem on Darwin/Windows.\r\n\r\nIt is definitely safer. And as far as I could tell, even more capable system file explorers/managers don't handle this very well. Probably for a good reason.",
